{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-daily-life-france-usa-japan/audio/main-12d126e9296b.mp3","durationSec":344.496,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.32,"text":"Imagine it is 12:30 in a French office."},{"start":3.06,"end":6.18,"text":"People stand up, close their computers and leave their desks."},{"start":7.08,"end":10.14,"text":"A visitor might think, \"The French just love to relax.\""},{"start":11.42,"end":13.2,"text":"But much of this comes from rules."},{"start":13.82,"end":16.78,"text":"In France, a full-time work week is 35 hours."},{"start":17.38,"end":20.7,"text":"If people work more, the extra hours count as overtime."},{"start":21.8,"end":23.48,"text":"There is also a rule about breaks."},{"start":24.56,"end":29.24,"text":"After 6 hours of work in a row, a worker must get a break of at least 20 minutes."},{"start":30.56,"end":31.62,"text":"Lunch can be this break."},{"start":32.56,"end":36.62,"text":"In practice, lunch is often longer, around 45 minutes."},{"start":37.76,"end":42.72,"text":"This time is usually unpaid, because the boss does not direct workers during lunch."},{"start":43.24,"end":45.84,"text":"So the lunch break really belongs to the worker."},{"start":46.92,"end":48.4,"text":"Big companies must also help."},{"start":49.02,"end":52.96,"text":"If a company has 50 or more workers, it must give them a room for eating."},{"start":53.74,"end":57.02,"text":"The room needs places to keep and heat food, and seats."},{"start":57.66,"end":58.92,"text":"The morning looks very different."},{"start":59.74,"end":65.2,"text":"A typical French breakfast is quick: bread with butter or jam, and a café au lait."},{"start":65.96,"end":68.64,"text":"So the day has a fast start and a protected middle."},{"start":69.42,"end":71.54,"text":"But the French day is not always short."},{"start":72.08,"end":74.72,"text":"The usual limit is 10 hours of work in one day."},{"start":75.54,"end":80.1,"text":"In special cases, such as a very busy period, it can go up to 12 hours."},{"start":80.68,"end":84.88,"text":"So the 35-hour week is a starting point, not a promise of easy days."},{"start":85.72,"end":86.92,"text":"Life is changing, too."},{"start":87.88,"end":93.1,"text":"Fast food and American eating habits put pressure on French food, especially for young people."},{"start":93.82,"end":97.36,"text":"Many French people still protect their food traditions through education and laws."},{"start":98.38,"end":100.42,"text":"Now imagine a morning in an American town."},{"start":101.14,"end":102.5,"text":"A woman gets into her car."},{"start":102.98,"end":107.58,"text":"She drives to work, stops at a window, orders coffee and food, and keeps driving."},{"start":108.08,"end":109.1,"text":"She never leaves her seat."},{"start":109.68,"end":111.54,"text":"This habit did not appear by chance."},{"start":112.06,"end":115.26,"text":"In the United States, many people use cars every day."},{"start":116.1,"end":120.9,"text":"Because so many people drove, drive-in and drive-through restaurants became popular."},{"start":121.56,"end":124.04,"text":"These restaurants changed daily eating habits."},{"start":124.98,"end":130.22,"text":"In 2014, the average American adult took 26.8 minutes to travel to work."},{"start":130.76,"end":135.08,"text":"That is a lot of time inside a car, and food fits easily into that time."},{"start":136.08,"end":140.84,"text":"Today, American food culture gives a big place to fast food and take-out meals."},{"start":141.72,"end":143.58,"text":"These meals come from many different cultures."},{"start":144.38,"end":151.7,"text":"Think of burgers, pizza, hot dogs, fried food, milkshakes, barbecue and Tex-Mex dishes."},{"start":152.7,"end":156.08,"text":"Many of these foods are easy to eat with your hands, even in a car."},{"start":157.16,"end":160.38,"text":"So the drive-through is not only about Americans \"loving to hurry\"."},{"start":160.92,"end":165.98,"text":"It is a smart answer to a simple fact: many people spend their day moving by car."},{"start":165.98,"end":169.18,"text":"If people come by car, the restaurant comes to the car window."},{"start":170.02,"end":172.2,"text":"In Japan, many people take a different path."},{"start":173.18,"end":176.7,"text":"In Tokyo, people usually travel to work by train, not by car."},{"start":177.66,"end":179.76,"text":"At lunch, someone may open a small box."},{"start":180.5,"end":185.06,"text":"Inside, there are several sections: rice, some fish or meat, and vegetables."},{"start":185.96,"end":186.76,"text":"This is a bento."},{"start":187.46,"end":190.56,"text":"A bento is a packed meal for one person, usually for lunch."},{"start":191.2,"end":195.54,"text":"It often has rice or noodles, fish or meat, and pickled or cooked vegetables."},{"start":196.28,"end":199,"text":"It looks like a small version of a traditional Japanese meal."},{"start":199.72,"end":205.44,"text":"That meal centers on rice and miso soup, with fish, pickled vegetables and cooked vegetables."},{"start":206.12,"end":207.82,"text":"These meals also follow the seasons."},{"start":209.14,"end":210.8,"text":"Why did people start carrying lunch?"},{"start":211.92,"end":214.42,"text":"Long ago, lunch was not a normal meal in Japan."},{"start":214.94,"end":217.72,"text":"It became common only in the early 18th century."},{"start":218.7,"end":221.82,"text":"Kerosene lamps let people stay awake and active for longer."},{"start":221.82,"end":225.78,"text":"Days grew longer, so people needed food in the middle."},{"start":225.78,"end":228.98,"text":"Workers started bringing bentos to work."},{"start":228.98,"end":231.34,"text":"Farmers had a practical problem."},{"start":231.88,"end":235.3,"text":"They worked far from home, so their food had to stay good when cold."},{"start":236.02,"end":238.22,"text":"They used wooden boxes called menpa."},{"start":238.82,"end":241.5,"text":"They filled them with barley rice and pickled plums."},{"start":242.06,"end":245.02,"text":"The wood kept the food fresh, even when it was cold."},{"start":245.76,"end":251.78,"text":"On very long days, like rice-planting days, villagers shared large wooden buckets of rice balls and side dishes."},{"start":252.88,"end":255.62,"text":"Bentos were also part of fun, not only work."},{"start":255.62,"end":258.82,"text":"Makunouchi bentos were served during breaks at the theater."},{"start":259.52,"end":262.58,"text":"They had grilled rice balls, fish cakes and simmered dishes."},{"start":263.16,"end":264.72,"text":"This style is still common today."},{"start":265.38,"end":267.28,"text":"So the bento is not just about being neat."},{"start":267.64,"end":271.28,"text":"It grew from longer days, distance from home and food that works cold."},{"start":271.86,"end":273.88,"text":"The land also changes what goes on the plate."},{"start":274.56,"end":279.02,"text":"Japan is a group of islands, and the sea is close to many people."},{"start":279.44,"end":282.92,"text":"This is why seafood is so important in Japanese food."},{"start":283.84,"end":285.92,"text":"Fish in a bento is not an accident."},{"start":286.38,"end":288.54,"text":"It reflects the sea around the country."},{"start":289.26,"end":291.04,"text":"The United States is very large."},{"start":291.62,"end":295.52,"text":"Because of this size, food and eating habits change from region to region."},{"start":295.96,"end":298.94,"text":"American food also grew more varied in the 20th century."},{"start":299.76,"end":303.98,"text":"Technology, wars, science and immigration all played a part."},{"start":304.62,"end":308.38,"text":"So \"American food\" is really many foods, not one."},{"start":308.38,"end":311.48,"text":"France shows the limits of this idea."},{"start":312.38,"end":316.08,"text":"French food has a long history, going back to the 14th century."},{"start":317.12,"end":319.34,"text":"Cheese and wine are big parts of it."},{"start":319.92,"end":322.38,"text":"The French place great value on enjoying food."},{"start":323.12,"end":328.32,"text":"Here, tradition, education and laws shape food as much as the land does."},{"start":329.2,"end":332.74,"text":"Even the lunch break comes from work rules, not from mountains or seas."},{"start":333.58,"end":338.32,"text":"So geography is a strong force, but it is one force among several."},{"start":338.32,"end":344.02,"text":"Laws, cars, lamps, distance and history all have a part."}],"words":[{"text":"Imagine","start":0,"end":0.36},{"text":"it","start":0.36,"end":0.62},{"text":"is","start":0.62,"end":0.8},{"text":"12","start":0.8,"end":1.11},{"text":"30","start":1.11,"end":1.42},{"text":"in","start":1.42,"end":1.64},{"text":"a","start":1.64,"end":1.76},{"text":"French","start":1.76,"end":1.92},{"text":"office","start":1.92,"end":2.32},{"text":"People","start":3.06,"end":3.26},{"text":"stand","start":3.26,"end":3.58},{"text":"up","start":3.58,"end":3.9},{"text":"close","start":4.14,"end":4.4},{"text":"their","start":4.4,"end":4.62},{"text":"computers","start":4.62,"end":4.98},{"text":"and","start":5.08,"end":5.4},{"text":"leave","start":5.4,"end":5.58},{"text":"their","start":5.58,"end":5.82},{"text":"desks","start":5.82,"end":6.18},{"text":"A","start":7.08,"end":7.22},{"text":"visitor","start":7.22,"end":7.46},{"text":"might","start":7.46,"end":7.7},{"text":"think","start":7.7,"end":8.08},{"text":"The","start":8.5,"end":8.7},{"text":"French","start":8.7,"end":8.96},{"text":"just","start":8.96,"end":9.26},{"text":"love","start":9.26,"end":9.54},{"text":"to","start":9.54,"end":9.78},{"text":"relax","start":9.78,"end":10.14},{"text":"But","start":11.42,"end":11.7},{"text":"much","start":11.7,"end":11.96},{"text":"of","start":11.96,"end":12.14},{"text":"this","start":12.14,"end":12.34},{"text":"comes","start":12.34,"end":12.58},{"text":"from","start":12.58,"end":12.86},{"text":"rules","start":12.86,"end":13.2},{"text":"In","start":13.82,"end":13.96},{"text":"France","start":13.96,"end":14.3},{"text"